ngthened  through the membership in the alliance  including turkey and we want to  strengthen alliance more through  two new member states sweden and finland  it is also in in the interest of turkey  in the interest of all nato member  states and therefore i am sure that  turkey and finland  and  sweden  will  solve the problems which they have and  at the end uh finland and sweden will  join nato and soon  so you're hopeful about a breakthrough  but but they are divisions too mr  president within the european union  hungary is blocking a six package of  sanctions against russia that includes a  russian oil ban  and i know your prime minister will be  attending a summit of eu leaders on this  can president obama be convinced how  would you convince him that this is the  way forward  we have already agreed five packages  including of course hungary has also  agreed with five packages of course uh  now there are negotiations about the  sixth package and uh i am sure that we  will come to result because all member  states of european union has their own  uh  their own views on that but we have a  common goal  the common goal is to sanction russia  in order to  keep peace in europe because the  sanctions is an instrument to  keep peace to get peace in europe a  common goal you say mr president but  these splits  perhaps are a signal that the unity that  we saw at the start of this crisis on  ukraine  and the unity that we've seen in the  last few months is a shaky one isn't it  the european union  is  unique i would say because this is a  completely new situation where we are  now  and uh  it is a  intended unintended side effect of  putin's politics that  we have now such a unity in the european  union and in nato in the western world  as a whole  and i would say that in order to  to stabilize this unity and to go  forward we need discussions and now it  is time to  for discussions in order to get the  results and i am sure that we will get  results right now with the 